  <article class="prose">
    <div class="mono-tag" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-2);">Regulatory &amp; Compliance Document</div>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <div class="prose-meta">
      Entity: HireScope Systems Inc. &bull; Effective Date: November 21, 2026 &bull; Domain: hirescope.io
    </div>

    <h2>1. Overview and Scope</h2>
    <p>
      HireScope Systems Inc. ("HireScope", "we", "us", or "our") operates the recruitment infrastructure at hirescope.io. This Privacy Policy outlines our principles and practices concerning the collection, utilization, processing, and protection of personal data gathered from job seekers, hiring managers, employer entities, and platform visitors.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Categories of Information Collected</h2>
    <p>
      We collect data strictly required to deliver direct, calibrated hiring infrastructure:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account Identification:</strong> Full name, verified email address, hashed passwords, telephone numbers, and geographic location bases.</li>
      <li><strong>Candidate Dossiers:</strong> Employment history, technical proficiencies, professional biographies, compensation preferences, cover pitches, and uploaded resume files (.pdf, .docx, .doc, .txt).</li>
      <li><strong>Employer Entity Metadata:</strong> Company name, registered domain, operational focus, hiring point contacts, and listing parameters.</li>
      <li><strong>System Telemetry:</strong> Minimal HTTP request headers, session cookies for authenticated session maintenance, and error diagnostics required for service stability. We do not use third-party tracking beacons or sell browsing telemetry.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Purpose and Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
    <p>
      We process your personal information under lawful bases including contractual necessity, legitimate business interests, and explicit consent:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Facilitating direct communication and application routing between candidates and hiring organizations.</li>
      <li>Validating account authenticity, access control, and platform security.</li>
      <li>Operating keyword indexing, taxonomy categorization, and faceted position search.</li>
      <li>Complying with statutory labor disclosures and data protection regulations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Disclosure of Information</h2>
    <p>
      HireScope does not sell, lease, or monetize candidate dossiers or employer contact details. Data is disclosed strictly within the following boundaries:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Direct Hiring Transmission:</strong> When a candidate explicitly submits an application for a position, their profile details, cover pitch, and uploaded resume are delivered to the employer managing that listing.</li>
      <li><strong>Legal Mandates:</strong> Where required by valid judicial subpoena, statutory law, or binding governmental order.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Data Security Infrastructure</h2>
    <p>
      We enforce technical safeguards designed to protect personal records against unauthorized access, loss, or alteration. All network transmissions are encrypted via modern TLS protocols. Passwords are cryptographically salted and hashed using bcrypt before persistent storage. Resume assets are stored in isolated system storage with strict file permission masks.
    </p>

    <h2 id="data-retention">6. Data Retention Policy</h2>
    <p>
      Candidate records and job postings remain stored for as long as the corresponding user account is active. Users possess the absolute right to purge their records at any time. When an account or listing is purged via the platform interface, all related applications, bookmarks, and files are permanently unlinked and destroyed from our active database.
    </p>

    <h2>7. User Rights and Controls</h2>
    <p>
      In accordance with applicable privacy frameworks (including GDPR and CCPA), you are entitled to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Access and review all personal data held in your account profile.</li>
      <li>Rectify inaccurate or outdated contact information via the Profile Settings console.</li>
      <li>Request permanent account deletion and erasure of submitted application records.</li>
      <li>Export account metadata in structured electronic format.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Contact Information</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy inquiries, data subject access requests, or regulatory questions, contact our designated Data Protection Officer at:
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>HireScope Systems Inc.</strong><br>
      Data Protection Office<br>
      Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@hirescope.io" style="color: var(--color-accent); font-weight: 600;">privacy@hirescope.io</a><br>
      Domain: hirescope.io
    </p>
